WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.870
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.140 --> 00:06.433
Akihiro Miyata,

3
00:08.324 --> 00:10.877
will you be my life partner?

4
00:25.180 --> 00:26.180
I'm sorry!

5
00:34.886 --> 00:36.286
I can't give an answer yet.

6
00:39.693 --> 00:41.117
Can I ask why?

7
00:44.436 --> 00:45.436
What did I...

8
00:47.799 --> 00:49.289
What did I do wrong?

9
00:55.013 --> 00:56.276
It's not you, Senpai.

10
00:57.527 --> 00:58.854
It's my problem.

11
01:11.695 --> 01:13.979
My head is a mess.

12
01:18.811 --> 01:19.811
What do you mean?

13
01:24.128 --> 01:26.230
Your book might fall through.

14
01:33.163 --> 01:38.918
Masumoto, the consultant, wants to rebuild the book around Biz-Bear.

15
01:40.722 --> 01:43.398
I think they'll contact you soon too.

16
01:48.052 --> 01:52.627
As the person in charge, I'm ashamed I couldn't protect your book.

17
01:53.804 --> 01:56.408
I don't have the headspace for anything else.

18
01:58.704 --> 02:00.521
Bad timing, huh?

19
02:01.794 --> 02:02.901
I'm sorry.

20
02:06.411 --> 02:08.060
I might...

21
02:09.384 --> 02:12.558
quit the company and go freelance.

22
02:13.370 --> 02:15.452
If that happens, of course I'll support you.

23
02:15.452 --> 02:16.842
Money's not an issue...

24
02:16.842 --> 02:18.113
Please don't do that.

25
02:22.581 --> 02:26.780
I want to earn enough to cover my own expenses.

26
02:30.488 --> 02:32.921
It might be foolish pride, but...

27
02:39.413 --> 02:40.413
No.

28
02:42.412 --> 02:43.412
That's fine.

29
02:46.990 --> 02:51.828
So, until everything is sorted out,

30
02:51.828 --> 02:53.369
can you wait for my answer?

31
03:14.871 --> 03:18.525
Maybe we both grew up too much.

32
03:22.778 --> 03:24.505
In these two years,

33
03:31.516 --> 03:34.025
I thought the distance between us had became nonexistent.

34
03:39.778 --> 03:41.020
Good night.

35
03:44.064 --> 03:45.064
Good night.

36
03:53.926 --> 03:57.252
I was a fool to believe that.

37
04:02.580 --> 04:05.254
Now you feel so far away.

38
05:08.582 --> 05:09.582
Takashi.

39
05:16.984 --> 05:17.984
Long time no see.

40
05:19.823 --> 05:20.823
Sota.

41
05:26.397 --> 05:28.537
You haven't changed at all.

42
05:28.537 --> 05:30.809
- You too. - Really?

43
05:31.510 --> 05:34.188
As you can see, I'm about to be buried in books.

44
05:34.959 --> 05:38.003
We're a small publisher run by three people.

45
05:38.003 --> 05:41.024
My staff keep telling me to be more business-minded.

46
05:41.692 --> 05:44.182
Still doing what you love, as always.

47
05:45.197 --> 05:48.228
In this day and age, it's almost ridiculous.

48
05:48.228 --> 05:52.283
No, it's good. That's just like you.

49
05:58.108 --> 06:01.735
Thanks for making time despite being busy.

50
06:02.632 --> 06:06.278
No, of course. I was glad you reached out.

51
06:08.153 --> 06:11.026
Me too. I'm glad to see you.

52
06:21.281 --> 06:22.561
Oh, I'll get it.

53
06:29.095 --> 06:32.859
So, um, Miyata...

54
06:32.859 --> 06:33.859
Yes?

55
06:34.612 --> 06:37.216
About Professor Iwanaga's book...

56
06:39.623 --> 06:41.773
Doesn't look good?

57
06:42.831 --> 06:47.648
Yeah, it looks like Masumoto's plan will go through.

58
06:49.983 --> 06:51.076
Understood.

59
06:55.283 --> 06:56.765
All right.

60
06:58.694 --> 06:59.694
Let's clock out.

61
07:01.004 --> 07:02.676
- Okay. - Mm-hmm.

62
07:04.201 --> 07:05.201
Let's go.

63
07:07.478 --> 07:10.805
Man, I talked about going freelance too,

64
07:10.805 --> 07:15.936
but my kid's about to take middle-school entrance exams, and money's tight.

65
07:15.936 --> 07:18.899
And who knows how long this industry will last?

66
07:21.737 --> 07:25.526
Jeez, I miss the days when books sold like crazy without doing anything.

67
07:25.526 --> 07:26.725
I know, right?

68
07:26.725 --> 07:28.658
Here are your crab cream croquettes.

69
07:28.658 --> 07:31.873
Oh, that's not mine. Maybe it's theirs.

70
07:31.873 --> 07:34.260
My apologies. Crab cream croquettes.

71
07:34.260 --> 07:36.171
Oh, sorry! Thank you.

72
07:36.171 --> 07:36.958
No problem.

73
07:36.958 --> 07:38.441
- Here. - Thank you.

74
07:38.441 --> 07:43.469
I happened to overhear your chat. Are you in publishing?

75
07:44.331 --> 07:45.753
Yes, that's right.

76
07:46.550 --> 07:47.988
So am I.

77
07:47.988 --> 07:50.353
Oh, a fellow colleague!

78
07:52.737 --> 07:54.304
That's nice.

79
07:55.783 --> 07:57.671
- Cheers! - Cheers!

80
08:00.439 --> 08:06.476
In the end, it's all about consumption, isn't it?

81
08:06.476 --> 08:09.064
I just can't keep up with that.

82
08:09.064 --> 08:11.209
No, I get it.

83
08:12.164 --> 08:16.297
Our company isn't about big sales either.

84
08:16.297 --> 08:20.752
We aim to work closely with authors and carefully craft each and every book.

85
08:22.035 --> 08:26.809
We want readers to become passionate fans who love these books deeply.

86
08:28.860 --> 08:31.838
Wow. That's completely different from our company.

87
08:31.838 --> 08:35.142
Well, we're small, so we have to do it that way.

88
08:35.142 --> 08:37.562
No, no, that's impressive.

89
08:37.562 --> 08:39.197
Here are your three waters.

90
08:39.197 --> 08:40.890
- Thank you. - Thank you.

91
08:42.418 --> 08:43.488
Please take your time.

92
08:47.867 --> 08:50.471
Miyata, have some water too.

93
08:51.284 --> 08:52.522
Thank you.

94
08:53.855 --> 08:56.558
- Hasegawa, you too, if you'd like. - Thank you.

95
09:07.443 --> 09:10.892
You must be happy having someone nice like that.

96
09:10.892 --> 09:12.986
Exactly!

97
09:16.126 --> 09:19.823
Arima, do you have a special someone?

98
09:24.546 --> 09:26.649
I did, back in college.

99
09:26.649 --> 09:30.335
But since we broke up, nothing's really clicked.

100
09:30.335 --> 09:31.922
You got dumped?

101
09:33.058 --> 09:36.385
No, I was the one who ended it.

102
09:36.385 --> 09:38.435
He was a wonderful person to the very end.

103
09:39.845 --> 09:41.545
And yet you dumped him?

104
09:42.548 --> 09:44.062
Some stuff happened.

105
09:44.062 --> 09:45.837
I see.

106
09:48.596 --> 09:51.974
Actually, I'm the same.

107
09:53.825 --> 09:58.606
My current partner and I were separated once,

108
09:59.730 --> 10:02.730
but we met again and started over.

109
10:02.730 --> 10:04.265
I'm surprised by that passion.

110
10:06.666 --> 10:08.423
So, Arima,

111
10:09.099 --> 10:14.162
if you still like that person, why not start over too?

112
10:17.381 --> 10:18.381
Thanks.

113
10:19.391 --> 10:23.030
Actually, recently, he came to see me.

114
10:24.226 --> 10:25.570
Maybe this is my chance.

115
10:25.570 --> 10:27.385
That's great!

116
10:28.779 --> 10:29.779
Yeah.

117
10:40.453 --> 10:43.160
To start, take a look at this.

118
10:44.739 --> 10:47.415
The new cover proposal.

119
10:47.415 --> 10:50.554
By putting Biz-Bear front and center like this,

120
10:50.554 --> 10:54.411
we believe we can reach a much larger readership.

121
10:54.411 --> 10:56.481
It's a highly marketable concept.

122
10:57.653 --> 11:01.032
As expected of you, Professor Iwanaga. Glad you understand.

123
11:02.662 --> 11:04.596
- Oh, then... - I decline.

124
11:10.611 --> 11:12.009
May I ask why?

125
11:13.697 --> 11:16.703
Miyata and I carefully crafted this book together.

126
11:16.703 --> 11:19.782
I refuse to rework it into something completely different.

127
11:19.782 --> 11:22.022
Even so...

128
11:22.022 --> 11:23.946
Please terminate our contract.

129
11:29.457 --> 11:32.944
I thought I had built a good relationship with Tokyo Business.

130
11:34.361 --> 11:36.087
It's truly regrettable.

131
11:38.840 --> 11:42.182
We sincerely apologize.

132
11:45.447 --> 11:47.175
That is unfortunate.

133
11:51.274 --> 11:53.661
I'll discuss the rest with Miyata alone.

134
11:57.421 --> 11:58.660
Excuse us.

135
12:07.199 --> 12:08.441
That surprised you, huh?

136
12:10.920 --> 12:12.799
This was for the best.

137
12:14.943 --> 12:17.477
But our book...

138
12:19.464 --> 12:20.988
There's still hope.

139
12:21.817 --> 12:23.320
Huh?

140
12:23.320 --> 12:28.036
If the contract is terminated, the publisher has no publication rights

141
12:28.036 --> 12:30.751
and the copyright returns to the author.

142
12:30.751 --> 12:35.052
In other words, I can publish this book with another publisher.

143
12:36.513 --> 12:38.213
But how do we find one?

144
12:39.572 --> 12:43.415
I've already talked to someone. Someone I trust deeply.

145
12:45.381 --> 12:48.016
But I can't be involved, can I?

146
12:50.974 --> 12:52.668
Not unless you go independent.

147
12:57.643 --> 13:02.610
[My thoughts after leaving my company three years ago to be a freelance editor.]

148
13:26.007 --> 13:27.007
Um...

149
13:28.632 --> 13:29.632
Tonight's a bit...

150
13:31.130 --> 13:32.130
Not tonight?

151
13:35.480 --> 13:37.150
I'm a little tired.

152
13:39.859 --> 13:40.859
I see.

153
13:42.249 --> 13:43.249
Another time.

154
13:44.885 --> 13:45.885
Yeah.

155
14:21.819 --> 14:25.025
He's a really openhearted guy, you know.

156
14:25.025 --> 14:27.358
The complete opposite of me.

157
14:27.358 --> 14:30.346
What are you saying? I'm sure you'll like him too, Miyata.

158
14:35.704 --> 14:36.704
Oh.

159
14:38.344 --> 14:39.988
Let me introduce you. This is...

160
14:42.275 --> 14:43.335
Arima?

161
14:43.335 --> 14:45.219
What? Miyata?

162
14:45.219 --> 14:47.699
Wait, you two know each other?

163
14:47.699 --> 14:50.849
We sat by each other at a pub recently and hit it off.

164
14:50.849 --> 14:52.979
- What a coincidence. - Right?

165
14:55.038 --> 14:56.038
Take a seat.

166
14:57.003 --> 14:59.231
Sota, I had no idea you met Miyata.

167
15:00.397 --> 15:02.405
That makes things quick.

168
15:02.405 --> 15:06.078
With Arima, I can entrust the book with peace of mind.

169
15:06.078 --> 15:07.526
Thank you.

170
15:07.526 --> 15:09.163
Not at all.

171
15:09.163 --> 15:13.663
Still, when I heard from Takashi, I thought, wow, that's a bold move.

172
15:14.928 --> 15:15.853
Yeah.

173
15:15.853 --> 15:17.968
But that's classic Takashi.

174
15:17.968 --> 15:20.037
Hm? What do you mean by that?

175
15:20.037 --> 15:21.887
Like our third year in college.

176
15:23.304 --> 15:24.304
Ah.

177
15:25.203 --> 15:27.876
You went to the same college?

178
15:27.876 --> 15:32.127
Yes. Actually, Takashi got into a fight with a senior in the debate club.

179
15:32.127 --> 15:34.518
So he started his own debate club.

180
15:34.518 --> 15:36.405
That makes me sound terrible.

181
15:36.405 --> 15:38.231
It was an academic disagreement.

182
15:38.231 --> 15:42.893
Then, at the next debate tournament, he beat all the seniors.

183
15:44.301 --> 15:45.915
He showed no mercy.

184
15:45.915 --> 15:48.425
I'd rather you didn't bring that up.

185
15:49.299 --> 15:53.780
But that's the kind of man he is, so I'm not surprised.

186
16:09.569 --> 16:12.631
Who gave you this watch?

187
16:13.686 --> 16:16.120
Someone I was close with in college.

188
16:16.120 --> 16:19.845
You've been wearing that watch a lot lately.

189
16:19.845 --> 16:22.143
Oh, the other one broke.

190
16:31.575 --> 16:34.939
Actually, recently, he came to see me.

191
16:35.924 --> 16:37.417
Maybe this is my chance.

192
16:37.417 --> 16:39.348
That's great!

193
16:43.258 --> 16:44.753
Let's talk about the book.

194
16:44.753 --> 16:46.066
Right, sorry.

195
16:47.329 --> 16:50.175
I gave Sota a broad outline,

196
16:50.175 --> 16:52.637
but did you want to ask anything, Miyata?

197
16:56.133 --> 16:57.133
Miyata?

198
16:59.368 --> 17:04.636
Sorry, I need to reconsider. Excuse me.

199
17:13.741 --> 17:14.774
Miyata!

200
17:48.292 --> 17:49.487
Takashi, is he...

201
18:02.145 --> 18:03.238
So, it was him.

202
18:56.715 --> 18:57.715
Miyata!

203
19:09.196 --> 19:10.249
Miyata?

204
19:19.213 --> 19:20.423
Were you two dating?

205
19:23.313 --> 19:24.326
You and Arima?

206
19:27.698 --> 19:28.698
Yeah.

207
19:30.660 --> 19:31.660
I thought so.

208
19:36.854 --> 19:38.481
He really is a wonderful person.

209
19:40.169 --> 19:43.021
Helping us even though he has no obligation to.

210
19:46.564 --> 19:53.044
You and Arima had a different vibe. You're a good match.

211
19:55.120 --> 19:56.851
He's just a friend.

212
19:57.721 --> 20:00.357
Besides, I got dumped, so...

213
20:00.357 --> 20:02.113
There can be a second time too,

214
20:03.437 --> 20:04.818
like for us.

215
20:18.398 --> 20:19.398
Sota...

216
20:21.158 --> 20:23.944
saved me when I was at rock bottom.

217
20:26.774 --> 20:28.379
Just because I'm with you,

218
20:30.696 --> 20:33.673
I can't throw away my entire past.

219
20:39.630 --> 20:41.428
Sorry for saying something stupid.

220
20:44.577 --> 20:48.962
I have no right, when I haven't even saved you once.

221
20:53.936 --> 20:56.000
Miyata, that's not what this is...

222
20:56.000 --> 20:57.195
When I'm with you,

223
20:58.572 --> 21:00.479
I start to hate myself.

224
21:05.115 --> 21:06.115
I...

225
21:09.049 --> 21:13.743
I kept getting jealous toward your exes, who all know a different side to you.

226
21:16.262 --> 21:18.006
I couldn't control it at all.

227
21:27.872 --> 21:30.306
Now I know what kind of person I am.

228
21:34.303 --> 21:35.724
Jealous.

229
21:40.659 --> 21:42.058
Petty.

230
21:43.695 --> 21:45.816
And cowardly.

231
21:48.392 --> 21:50.106
I've been forced to realize that.

232
21:54.988 --> 21:59.365
Even you can't argue with that, can you, Professor Iwanaga?

233
22:08.368 --> 22:09.983
You think that's how I see you?

234
22:19.885 --> 22:21.009
That's impossible.

235
22:22.992 --> 22:25.154
I love you so much.

236
22:35.198 --> 22:36.587
Won't you believe me?

237
22:44.173 --> 22:45.466
I don't think I can.

238
22:52.002 --> 22:54.042
Please just forget about me.

239
22:58.723 --> 22:59.926
I think...

240
23:02.167 --> 23:04.351
we'll both be happier that way.

241
23:12.853 --> 23:14.299
There won't be...

242
23:16.804 --> 23:17.804
a third time.

243
23:36.750 --> 23:37.938
You two broke up, huh?

244
23:37.938 --> 23:40.895
I don't need to feel guilty about it, right?

245
23:40.895 --> 23:44.551
How dare you make the professor cry, you nobody.

246
23:44.551 --> 23:45.884
You damn bitch.

247
23:45.884 --> 23:47.413
Ooh la la!

248
23:47.413 --> 23:49.206
You left me behind.

249
23:49.206 --> 23:50.251
Why?

250
23:50.251 --> 23:52.170
It's because I didn't say why.

251
23:53.028 --> 23:54.289
Senpai, wait!

252
23:54.289 --> 23:57.758
I'm not strong enough to endure it over and over either.

253
23:57.758 --> 23:59.793
If only you'd told me then.
